-- title:
--   Ramification index equals inertia order at every conjugate
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field and $G$ a finite group acting faithfully on $F$ by ring automorphisms. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $F$ whose underlying ring is a discrete valuation ring, and write $P^\flat = P \cap F^{G}$ for the pullback of $P$ along the inclusion of the subfield of $G$-fixed points, a valuation subring of $F^{G}$; assume its residue field is perfect. Let $n$ be a natural number equal to the cardinality of the set of $h \in G$ such that $h \cdot P = P$ and, for every $e \in P$, the difference $h \cdot e - e$ lies in `P.nonunits`, i.e. belongs to $P$ and is not a unit of $P$ (so $n$ is the order of the inertia group of $P$). The assertion is then: for every $g \in G$, every valuation subring $Q$ of $F$ with $Q = g \cdot P$, and every ring homomorphism $j : P^{\flat} \to Q$ that respects the underlying elements of $F$ (the image in $F$ of $j(r)$ equals the image in $F$ of $r$ for all $r$), the ideal of $Q$ generated by the image under $j$ of the maximal ideal of $P^{\flat}$ equals the $n$-th power of the maximal ideal of $Q$.
--
--   This is the statement $e(Q \mid P^{\flat}) = |I_{P}|$ of Hilbert ramification theory for the extension $F/F^{G}$, in a form transported to all conjugates $Q = g \cdot P$ of $P$ and to an arbitrary inclusion-compatible map $P^{\flat} \to Q$. It feeds the identification of place widths with inertia orders on integral models of the modular curves $X_0$, where the place of $F$ lying below a chosen place is only known up to conjugacy.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_map_maximalIdeal_comap_fixedPoints_eq_pow_of_eq_smul_of_natCard_eq.lean

